.TH "GENI\-UPLOADER" "1" "October 2026" "geni-uploader 1.0.0" "Geni Uploader Manual"
.SH NAME
geni\-uploader \- user\-run uploader for Geni source documents and photos
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B geni\-uploader [\-\-token\-file TOKEN_FILE] COMMAND [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
geni\-uploader uploads source documents and photos to Geni profiles through Geni's official API, from a manifest in a private data repository, and verifies every write with a follow\-up GET. It runs as a container image that carries the reviewed code; the data repository is cloned at run time and credentials are mounted at run time, so neither is baked into the image, printed, or committed.
.PP
Every network call passes an allowlist of (method, kind) pairs. GETs retry on transient errors; POSTs are never blindly retried. Logs never contain tokens, headers, payloads, or personal names: items are logged as short hashes.
.PP
The details\-* commands maintain metadata of sources that already exist on Geni; they never create or delete anything.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B auth\-url
generate the Geni OAuth authorization URL
.TP
.B whoami
verify Geni API credentials and print the authenticated profile
.TP
.B plan
dry\-run a manifest against live Geni state without writing
.TP
.B run
upload manifest sources to Geni with journaled, verified writes
.TP
.B contrast
compare Geni server listings against the manifest
.TP
.B guidmap
map the manifest's profile IDs to resolved API identifiers
.TP
.B pguid
print each profile's resolved API identifier
.TP
.B listing\-shape
print the JSON shape of profile document/photo listings
.TP
.B details-validate
validate the source\-details manifest schema
.TP
.B details-plan
plan existing\-source metadata repairs
.TP
.B details-repair
apply reviewed metadata repairs to existing sources
.TP
.B details-snapshot
snapshot existing\-source metadata to a private file
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GENI_UPLOAD_REPO
https URL of the private data repository the loader clones
.TP
.B GENI_UPLOAD_REF
branch of the data repository to clone (default: its HEAD)
.TP
.B GENI_UPLOAD_EXPECT_SHA
expected HEAD commit of the data repository (fails closed)
.TP
.B GH_TOKEN_FILE
path of the mounted GitHub token file (default: /run/gh\-token)
.TP
.B GENI_API_BASE
Geni API base URL override; the allowlist still applies
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /run/gh\-token
mounted GitHub token for repository sync (never logged)
.TP
.B /run/geni\-token
mounted Geni access token (never logged)
.TP
.B geni\-upload\-state.json
default durable upload state file
.TP
.B geni\-upload\-run.log
default run diagnostic log, next to the state file
.TP
.B upload\-status.yaml
status file committed and pushed back to the data repository
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the command completed
.TP
.B 1
failure (see the diagnostic log)
.TP
.B 2
refused (for example a missing \-\-confirm YES)
.TP
.B 3
uncertain items remain; review them on Geni before re\-running
.TP
.B 4
identity or tag verification stopped the run
.TP
.B 5
uploads are verified on Geni; only the repository status push failed
.TP
.B 6
another run holds the state lock
